My PDF Bot (RAG Chatbot) 🤖📄
A lightweight Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline built using Python, LangChain, and FAISS to query and extract precise answers from PDF documents.

🚀 Features
Automated PDF Ingestion: Dynamically fetches and loads PDF documents.

Smart Text Chunking: Splits large documents into optimized semantic chunks using RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.

Vector Embeddings: Converts text into numerical vectors using HuggingFace (all-MiniLM-L6-v2).

Fast Similarity Search: Uses FAISS vector database for high-speed context retrieval based on user queries.

🛠️ Tech Stack
Python

Google Colab

LangChain / LangChain-Text-Splitters

FAISS (Facebook AI Similarity Search)

HuggingFace Transformers

📌 Step-by-Step Implementation Flow
Environment Setup & Dependencies: Installed required packages (langchain, pypdf, faiss-cpu, sentence-transformers, langchain-text-splitters).

PDF Loading: Loaded the target document into the Python environment using PyPDFLoader.

Text Chunking: Divided the raw text into manageable pieces (chunk_size=500, chunk_overlap=50) to preserve contextual meaning.

Vector Database Creation: Generated vector embeddings and stored them in a local FAISS vector store.

Retrieval & Querying: Executed semantic similarity searches (similarity_search) to pull exact context relevant to user prompts.

